<BaseLayout title="How this site is built" description="A bit about the infrastructure behind the site" lang="en">
  <p class="eyebrow">A bit behind the scenes</p>
  <h1>How this site is built</h1>

  <p>
    The site is built with <a href="https://astro.build" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Astro</a>,
    hosted as a static site on Cloudflare Pages, with images hosted on
    Cloudflare R2 and served through <code>media.matanbrown.com</code>.
  </p>

  <p>
    Every page exists in two versions — Hebrew and English — with the
    exact same path structure (<code>/practices/x/</code> vs.
    <code>/en/practices/x/</code>), so a link to the Hebrew version can
    always find its English twin, and vice versa.
  </p>

  <p>
    Search on the site doesn't rely on an external service — it's built
    with <a href="https://pagefind.app" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Pagefind</a>,
    which builds a static search index at build time and runs entirely
    in the browser, with no server and no ongoing cost.
  </p>

  <p>
    Some of the content here was written with the help of Claude — both
    directly in conversation, and through an automated process: twice a
    week, a topic is pulled from a list I prepare in advance, Claude
    drafts it in Hebrew and English, and opens a Pull Request for it on
    GitHub. Nothing publishes automatically — I read it, edit if needed,
    and only then publish it myself.
  </p>

  <p>
    The contact form and the update signup form are protected by
    <a href="https://developers.cloudflare.com/turnstile/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Cloudflare Turnstile</a>
    (an invisible CAPTCHA) to block bots, and all submissions go through
    my own Cloudflare Function — not a third-party form service.
  </p>

  <p><a href="/en/">← Back to homepage</a></p>
</BaseLayout>
